  "qualifications": [
    "All coherent cohort20 runtime proof is private; no official20 or platform-complete claim.",
    "Browser facade uses Intl and navigator.languages; native facade uses .NET CultureInfo/TimeZoneInfo and exposes CurrentUICulture as a singleton, not an OS preferred-language list.",
    "Application overrides never mutate navigator, process cultures, OS preferences or system time zone.",
    "Canonicalization is provider qualified: native may preserve iw-IL and US/Eastern; Chromium normalizes them to he-IL and America/New_York.",
    "Sage bare session globalization is invariant; actual .NET provider behavior was checked through compiler/native CLI fallback.",
    "Initial AOT setup errors NETSDK1207 and unset MSBuild OS were corrected by target-framework narrowing and child-only OS=Windows_NT; no global environment change.",
    "AOT retains dependency/trim warnings from FSharp.Core and existing SameValueZero reflection; native JIT build is 0 warnings and 0 errors.",
    "The configured analyzer pipeline initially lacked existing private build/docs dependencies. Exact cached artifacts were copied and hashed into an owned feed; no source or tool versions changed.",
    "The first full Chromium execution followed a refused test-suite lease while the build lease was held. The completed valid runtime result is retained; actual granted-only callback guard/refused sentinel proof and subsequent proper lease handling are explicit in the deviation receipt.",
    "Official producer pin replacement, four-platform hosted source gates and normal/traced official package execution remain required before H06 acceptance."
